<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 566 0 R
/T (An agent's ability to reason well depends not just on the quality of its LLM, but on what information it can access at the moment of reasoning. Memory is the mechanism that makes information available across time -beyond the narrow window of a single LLM call. Without a well-designed memory architecture, even the most capable model is effectively amnesiac: it can only reason about what fits in its current context, and it forgets everything the moment the context is cleared. )
/E (An agent's ability to reason well depends not just on the quality of its LLM, but on what information it can access at the moment of reasoning. Memory is the mechanism that makes information available across time -beyond the narrow window of a single LLM call. Without a well-designed memory architecture, even the most capable model is effectively amnesiac: it can only reason about what fits in its current context, and it forgets everything the moment the context is cleared. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
