1159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 567 0 R
/T (Diagram description: The four memory tiers form a hierarchy. Working Memory is the active context -the smallest and fastest tier, holding only what the agent is currently reasoning about. When Working Memory overflows, content is summarized and written to Episodic Memory. Semantic Memory holds large-scale external knowledge and feeds relevant documents into Working Memory via RAG retrieval. Procedural Memory stores reusable action sequences and policies, retrieved on demand. All three long-term tiers ultimately surface their content through Working Memory -the only tier the LLM directly reads. )
/E (Diagram description: The four memory tiers form a hierarchy. Working Memory is the active context -the smallest and fastest tier, holding only what the agent is currently reasoning about. When Working Memory overflows, content is summarized and written to Episodic Memory. Semantic Memory holds large-scale external knowledge and feeds relevant documents into Working Memory via RAG retrieval. Procedural Memory stores reusable action sequences and policies, retrieved on demand. All three long-term tiers ultimately surface their content through Working Memory -the only tier the LLM directly reads. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
