/T (For agents that operate across multiple sessions -a coding assistant that remembers your project, a customer service agent that recalls prior tickets -episodic memory must be persisted to durable storage. The typical implementation uses a key-value store or relational database keyed by session ID or user ID. At the start of each session, the agent retrieves the relevant episodic record and loads it into Working Memory.)
