/T (Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is the primary mechanism for grounding an agent in external knowledge. It addresses a fundamental limitation of LLMs: their knowledge is frozen at training time. A model trained in early 2024 knows nothing about events after that date, and it may have incomplete or incorrect knowledge about specialized domains even within its training window. )
/E (Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is the primary mechanism for grounding an agent in external knowledge. It addresses a fundamental limitation of LLMs: their knowledge is frozen at training time. A model trained in early 2024 knows nothing about events after that date, and it may have incomplete or incorrect knowledge about specialized domains even within its training window. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
