/T (Chain-of-Thought prompting is a technique for improving the quality of LLM reasoning by instructing the model to produce an explicit step-by-step reasoning trace before arriving at a final answer. Rather than jumping directly from question to answer, the model "thinks out loud" -working through intermediate steps, checking its logic, and building toward a conclusion incrementally.)
/E (Chain-of-Thought prompting is a technique for improving the quality of LLM reasoning by instructing the model to produce an explicit step-by-step reasoning trace before arriving at a final answer. Rather than jumping directly from question to answer, the model "thinks out loud" -working through intermediate steps, checking its logic, and building toward a conclusion incrementally.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
