/T (Never let tool errors silently propagate as empty or null results. An agent that receives an empty result from a failed tool call may conclude "there are no results" and proceed on a false premise. Always distinguish between "the tool returned no results" and "the tool call failed" -these require completely different responses from the Reasoning Engine.)
