/P 601 0 R
/E (a process that exposes tools, resources, and prompts over the MCP protocol. An MCP server might wrap a database, a file system, a web search API, a code execution environment, or any other capability. Servers are standalone processes that communicate over stdio or HTTP/SSE. )
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [10]
>>
