1844 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 601 0 R
/T (Before MCP, integrating a new tool into an agent required writing custom adapter code for each framework. With MCP, a tool author writes one MCP server and any MCP-compatible agent can use it immediately. This creates a composable ecosystem: agents can mix and match tools from different providers without integration overhead.)
/E (Before MCP, integrating a new tool into an agent required writing custom adapter code for each framework. With MCP, a tool author writes one MCP server and any MCP-compatible agent can use it immediately. This creates a composable ecosystem: agents can mix and match tools from different providers without integration overhead.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
1845 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 601 0 R
/T (MCP also standardizes the security model. MCP servers declare their capabilities explicitly, and MCP clients can enforce allow-lists, rate limits, and parameter validation at the protocol layer -before tool calls reach the underlying implementation.)
/E (MCP also standardizes the security model. MCP servers declare their capabilities explicitly, and MCP clients can enforce allow-lists, rate limits, and parameter validation at the protocol layer -before tool calls reach the underlying implementation.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
1846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 601 0 R
/T (MCP is an evolving standard. As of 2025, it has broad adoption among major LLM providers and agent frameworks, but the specification continues to develop. When building production systems, pin to a specific MCP version and monitor the changelog for breaking changes. The core concepts -server/client separation, JSON Schema tool definitions, resource/tool/prompt distinction -are stable and worth designing around even if specific protocol details evolve.)
/E (MCP is an evolving standard. As of 2025, it has broad adoption among major LLM providers and agent frameworks, but the specification continues to develop. When building production systems, pin to a specific MCP version and monitor the changelog for breaking changes. The core concepts -server/client separation, JSON Schema tool definitions, resource/tool/prompt distinction -are stable and worth designing around even if specific protocol details evolve.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
