/T (Structural Separation is the most effective single mitigation. Wrapping external content in explicit XML-like tags and including a system prompt instruction that content inside those tags is data -not instructions -significantly reduces \(though does not eliminate\) the LLM's tendency to follow injected instructions.)
/E (Structural Separation is the most effective single mitigation. Wrapping external content in explicit XML-like tags and including a system prompt instruction that content inside those tags is data -not instructions -significantly reduces \(though does not eliminate\) the LLM's tendency to follow injected instructions.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
