/T (Online evaluation \(running evaluators against live traffic\) gives you a real-time quality signal, but it has limitations: you can only evaluate what users actually ask, you cannot safely test failure modes in production, and you cannot measure regression -whether a new agent version is better or worse than the previous one. Offline evaluation addresses these gaps by running the agent against a curated, static dataset of test cases before deployment. )
/E (Online evaluation \(running evaluators against live traffic\) gives you a real-time quality signal, but it has limitations: you can only evaluate what users actually ask, you cannot safely test failure modes in production, and you cannot measure regression -whether a new agent version is better or worse than the previous one. Offline evaluation addresses these gaps by running the agent against a curated, static dataset of test cases before deployment. )
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [10]
>>
