/T (Moving an agent from prototype to production is not a matter of flipping a switch -it is a distinct engineering effort that addresses reliability, operability, cost, and safety at a scale and rigor that prototypes never require. A prototype proves that an agent can do something. A production system proves that it will do it reliably, safely, and economically, day after day, under conditions the prototype never encountered. )
/E (Moving an agent from prototype to production is not a matter of flipping a switch -it is a distinct engineering effort that addresses reliability, operability, cost, and safety at a scale and rigor that prototypes never require. A prototype proves that an agent can do something. A production system proves that it will do it reliably, safely, and economically, day after day, under conditions the prototype never encountered. )
/Pg 124 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
