/T (Do not expose a prototype agent to real users under the assumption that you will "harden it later." Prototype agents lack the error handling, cost controls, and safety layers that production requires. A single runaway agent run can exhaust an API quota, expose sensitive data, or take an irreversible action. Treat the prototype-to-production transition as a first-class engineering milestone.)
/E (Do not expose a prototype agent to real users under the assumption that you will "harden it later." Prototype agents lack the error handling, cost controls, and safety layers that production requires. A single runaway agent run can exhaust an API quota, expose sensitive data, or take an irreversible action. Treat the prototype-to-production transition as a first-class engineering milestone.)
/Pg 125 0 R
/K [4]
