/Title (Diagram description: The four memory tiers form a hierarchy. Working Memory is the active context -the smallest and fastest tier, holding only what the agent is currently reasoning about. When Working Memory overflows, content is summarized and written to Episodic Memory. Semantic Memory holds large-scale external knowledge and feeds relevant documents into Working Memory via RAG retrieval. Procedural Memory stores reusable action sequences and policies, retrieved on demand. All three long-term tiers ultimately surface their content through Working Memory -the only tier the LLM directly reads.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 10658 0 R
/Prev 10676 0 R
/First 10677 0 R
