<<
/Title (A general-purpose agent is a generalist. For complex domains -legal analysis, financial modeling, security auditing, code generation in a specific language -a specialized agent with a domain-specific system prompt, curated tools, and fine-tuned behavior will consistently outperform a generalist. Multi-agent systems allow you to compose specialists: route legal questions to the legal agent, code questions to the code agent, and let an orchestrator manage the routing.)
